:"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-17T14:26:13Z","updated_at":"2021-10-17T14:26:13Z","body":"If i'm at the wrong spot, please correct me.\r\n\r\nWe have switched out FTP-Server and the new one makes TLS session reuse mandatory.\r\nThis works great with most clients.\r\nHowever we have a CentOS7 server that is not able to connect to the data channel.\r\nIt has the following curl version:\r\n`curl 7.29.0 (x86_64-redhat-linux-gnu) libcurl/7.29.0 NSS/3.53.1 zlib/1.2.7 libidn/1.28 libssh2/1.8.0`\r\nWhen trying to connect to the data channel it says:\r\n`< 425 Unable to build data connection: TLS session of data connection not resumed.`\r\n`* server did not report OK, got 425`\r\n\r\nThis is working fine with the local installation of curl on my mac with the following version:\r\n`curl 7.64.1 (x86_64-apple-darwin20.0) libcurl/7.64.1 (SecureTransport) LibreSSL/2.8.3 zlib/1.2.11 nghttp2/1.41.0`\r\n\r\nIn wich version was this fixed? I am not sure if i am looking in the right place because the entry from https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/6be2804cdceee1664bd970c184f14f8297374909 is still there on the latest tag of curl which is far newer than my local installation.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/945134803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Brm-Bremen","id":32572013,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTcyMDEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32572013?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brm-Bremen","html_url":"https://github.com/Brm-Bremen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brm-Bremen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brm-Bremen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brm-Bremen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brm-Bremen/starred{